 "name": "Urumqi Street Scenes: Six Perceptions (1–10)",
 "description": "Method replication: participants rate 20 street scenes from the Hongshan central district of Urumqi on the six Place Pulse perceptions (safety, liveliness, beauty, wealthiness, depressiveness, boringness) from 1 to 10, with an optional comment at the end. The images are not the paper's stimuli (47 Baidu street views fetched for this template, four directions joined into a 360° strip with the car roof cropped, 2021–2023 captures).\n\nOriginal study: Yao, Dall'Ò & Lu (2026), \"Urban Street-Scene Perception and Renewal Strategies Powered by Vision–Language Models\", Land 15(2), 244. Vision–language models scored 4,215 Baidu panoramas of the district; to validate them, 500 respondents each rated a random set of 40 of 800 sampled images on a 10-point scale (1 = very negative, 10 = very positive) for the six dimensions, and 156 also left comments.\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) 20 images per participant instead of 40; (2) the scale ends read \"very low\" and \"very high\" for every dimension, so depressiveness and boringness are rated as they are (invert them before averaging, as the paper did); (3) the model scoring and renewal recommendations are not part of the template.",
